IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sgta-nouns`

-- Telecommunications Act 1999 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (TA1999.txt).
-- PART 2: s 11(2) to (7) (the rest of approval of equipment), s 12 (residual power of the Authority), s 13 (charges for
-- services provided by the Authority), s 14 (sharing of radio frequency spectrum).  s 11(1) is in sgta-s11-approval.l4.
-- 2000 Revised Edition numbers: s 11 was s 9, s 12 was s 10, s 13 was s 11, s 14 was s 11A.

§ `s 11(2) to (7): approval of equipment`

-- src:1195 | (2) A person applying for an approval under this section may be
-- src:1196 | required by the Authority to comply with such requirements as the
-- src:1197 | Authority may think appropriate; and those requirements may include
-- src:1198 | a requirement to satisfy some other person with respect to any matter.
@ref s 11(2) (src:1195-1198)
GIVEN `the person applies for an approval under section 11` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requirement is one the Authority thinks appropriate (it may include a requirement to satisfy some other person about a matter)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(2): the Authority may require the applicant to comply with this requirement` MEANS
    `the person applies for an approval under section 11` AND `the requirement is one the Authority thinks appropriate (it may include a requirement to satisfy some other person about a matter)`

-- src:1200 | (3) An approval under this section may apply either to particular
-- src:1201 | equipment or to any equipment of a description specified in the
-- src:1202 | approval, and may so apply either for the purposes of a particular
-- src:1203 | telecommunication system or for the purposes of any
-- src:1204 | telecommunication system of a description so specified.
@ref s 11(3) (src:1200-1204)
GIVEN `the approval specifies particular equipment, or equipment of a description specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the approval is for the purposes of a particular telecommunication system, or any telecommunication system of a description specified in it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(3): the approval applies to the equipment and the system` MEANS
    `the approval specifies particular equipment, or equipment of a description specified in it` AND `the approval is for the purposes of a particular telecommunication system, or any telecommunication system of a description specified in it`

-- src:1206 | (4) An approval under this section may specify conditions which
-- src:1207 | must be complied with if the approval is to apply, for any purposes
-- src:1208 | specified in the approval, to any telecommunication system or
-- src:1209 | equipment which is so specified or is of a description so specified.
@ref s 11(4) (src:1206-1209)
GIVEN `the equipment or system is specified in the approval or is of a description so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conditions specified in the approval are complied with` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(4): the approval applies to the equipment or system for the purposes specified in the approval` MEANS
    `the equipment or system is specified in the approval or is of a description so specified` AND `the conditions specified in the approval are complied with`

-- src:1214 | (5) Any such condition referred to in subsection (4) may impose on
-- src:1215 | the person to whom the approval is given a requirement from time to
-- src:1216 | time to satisfy some other person with respect to any matter.
@ref s 11(5) (src:1214-1216)
GIVEN `the condition requires the person to whom the approval is given to satisfy some other person about a matter from time to time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(5): the approval may include this condition` MEANS
    `the condition requires the person to whom the approval is given to satisfy some other person about a matter from time to time`

-- src:1218 | (6) The Authority or any other person by whom any matter falls to
-- src:1219 | be determined for the purposes of any requirement imposed pursuant
-- src:1220 | to subsection (2) or (4) may charge a fee in respect of the carrying out
-- src:1221 | of any test or other assessment made by the Authority or other person.
@ref s 11(6) (src:1218-1221)
GIVEN `the fee is for the carrying out of a test or other assessment of a matter determined for the purposes of a requirement under subsection (2) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(6): the Authority or other person may charge a fee for the test or assessment` MEANS
    `the fee is for the carrying out of a test or other assessment of a matter determined for the purposes of a requirement under subsection (2) or (4)`

-- src:1223 | (7) A public telecommunication licensee may, with the approval of
-- src:1224 | the Authority (except in cases of emergency), cease or refuse to
-- src:1225 | supply a telecommunication service to any person by means of a
-- src:1226 | telecommunication system operated by the licensee if, through the
-- src:1227 | use of such telecommunication service, there is or is intended to be
-- src:1228 | connected to the telecommunication system, equipment or cabling
-- src:1229 | that is a threat to —
-- src:1231 | (a) the safety or proper functioning of the telecommunication
-- src:1232 | system; or
-- src:1234 | (b) the safety of any person.
@ref s 11(7) (src:1223-1234)
GIVEN `the Authority approved the cessation or refusal, or it is a case of emergency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `through the use of the service there is or is intended to be connected to the system equipment or cabling that is a threat to the safety or proper functioning of the telecommunication system` IS A BOOLEAN
      `through the use of the service there is or is intended to be connected to the system equipment or cabling that is a threat to the safety of a person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 11(7): the public telecommunication licensee may cease or refuse to supply the telecommunication service to the person` MEANS
    `the Authority approved the cessation or refusal, or it is a case of emergency` AND (`through the use of the service there is or is intended to be connected to the system equipment or cabling that is a threat to the safety or proper functioning of the telecommunication system` OR `through the use of the service there is or is intended to be connected to the system equipment or cabling that is a threat to the safety of a person`)

§ `s 12 Residual power of Authority to provide telecommunication services`

-- src:1243 | 12.—(1) The Authority may provide any telecommunication
-- src:1244 | service even though it has granted a licence to any person under
-- src:1245 | section 5, in any of the following circumstances:
-- src:1247 | (a) if the Authority is of the opinion that a person licensed
-- src:1248 | under section 5 has failed to discharge or is not discharging
-- src:1249 | to the Authority’s satisfaction the obligations imposed by
-- src:1250 | the Authority on the person in the licence granted to the
-- src:1251 | person;
-- src:1253 | (b) to give effect to any direction of the Minister under
-- src:1254 | section 77.
@ref s 12(1) (src:1243-1254)
GIVEN `the Authority is of the opinion that a person licensed under section 5 has failed to discharge, or is not discharging to its satisfaction, the obligations imposed in the licence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority provides the service to give effect to a direction of the Minister under section 77` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(1): the Authority may provide the telecommunication service even though it has granted a licence under section 5` MEANS
    `the Authority is of the opinion that a person licensed under section 5 has failed to discharge, or is not discharging to its satisfaction, the obligations imposed in the licence` OR `the Authority provides the service to give effect to a direction of the Minister under section 77`

-- src:1256 | (2) Where the Authority undertakes the provision of
-- src:1257 | telecommunication services under subsection (1), sections 2, 11, 15
-- src:1258 | to 28, 29(1), 36, 59 to 63, 65 to 76 and 93 apply, with the necessary
-- src:1260 | Informal Consolidation – version in force from 2/10/2026
-- src:1261 | 2020 Ed. Telecommunications Act 1999 26
-- src:1263 | modifications, to the Authority in respect of the provision of such
-- src:1264 | services and the references to public telecommunication licensee in
-- src:1265 | those sections are to be read as references to the Authority.
@ref s 12(2) (src:1256-1265)
GIVEN section IS A STRING
      `the Authority undertakes the provision of telecommunication services under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 12(2): this section applies to the Authority, with the necessary modifications, in respect of those services` MEANS
    `the Authority undertakes the provision of telecommunication services under subsection (1)`
    AND elem section (LIST "2", "11", "15 to 28", "29(1)", "36", "59 to 63", "65 to 76", "93")

§ `s 13 Charges and other terms for services provided by Authority`

-- src:1271 | 13.—(1) The Authority may make, in relation to any service
-- src:1272 | provided by the Authority under this Act, a scheme or schemes for
-- src:1273 | determining either or both of the following:
-- src:1275 | (a) the charges which, except insofar as they are the subject of
-- src:1276 | an agreement between the Authority and a person making
-- src:1277 | use of the service, are to be made by the Authority;
-- src:1279 | (b) the other terms and conditions which, except as provided,
-- src:1280 | are to be applicable to the service.
@ref s 13(1) (src:1271-1280)
GIVEN `the service is provided by the Authority under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1): the Authority may make a scheme determining the charges, or the other terms and conditions, applicable to the service` MEANS
    `the service is provided by the Authority under this Act`

-- src:1282 | (2) A scheme made under this section may make different provision
-- src:1283 | for different cases or classes of cases determined by, or in accordance
-- src:1284 | with, the provisions of the scheme.
@ref s 13(2) (src:1282-1284)
GIVEN `the scheme makes different provision for different cases or classes of cases determined by, or in accordance with, its provisions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(2): the scheme may make that different provision` MEANS
    `the scheme makes different provision for different cases or classes of cases determined by, or in accordance with, its provisions`

-- src:1286 | (3) A charge exigible by virtue of this section may be recovered by
-- src:1287 | the Authority in any court of competent jurisdiction as if it were a
-- src:1288 | simple contract debt.
@ref s 13(3) (src:1286-1288)
GIVEN `the charge is exigible by virtue of section 13` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(3): the Authority may recover the charge in any court of competent jurisdiction as if it were a simple contract debt` MEANS
    `the charge is exigible by virtue of section 13`

-- src:1290 | (4) A scheme or any amendment of the scheme made under this
-- src:1291 | section comes into operation on such date as may be determined by
-- src:1292 | the Authority.
@ref s 13(4) (src:1290-1292)
GIVEN `the date has been determined by the Authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date is on or after the date the Authority determined` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(4): the scheme or its amendment is in operation` MEANS
    `the date has been determined by the Authority` AND `the date is on or after the date the Authority determined`

-- src:1294 | (5) This section does not prohibit the Authority from levying any
-- src:1295 | charge or collecting any dues for anything done or any service
-- src:1296 | rendered by reason only of not being incorporated in a scheme, and
-- src:1297 | the rates, charges and fees payable to the Authority for any service
-- src:1298 | rendered must be in accordance with such rates, charges and fees as
-- src:1299 | may be determined by the Authority.
@ref s 13(5) (src:1294-1299)
GIVEN `the charge or dues are for a thing done or a service rendered that is not incorporated in a scheme` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(5): the Authority may levy the charge or collect the dues at the rate it determines` MEANS
    `the charge or dues are for a thing done or a service rendered that is not incorporated in a scheme`

-- src:1301 | (6) The rates, charges and fees applied by the TAS immediately
-- src:1302 | before 1 December 1999 continue to be valid as though determined
-- src:1303 | by the Authority under this section until rescinded, varied or
-- src:1304 | otherwise determined by the Authority.
@ref s 13(6) (src:1301-1304)
GIVEN `the rate, charge or fee was applied by the TAS immediately before 1 December 1999` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Authority has rescinded, varied or otherwise determined it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(6): the rate, charge or fee continues to be valid as though determined by the Authority` MEANS
    `the rate, charge or fee was applied by the TAS immediately before 1 December 1999` AND (NOT `the Authority has rescinded, varied or otherwise determined it`)

§ `s 14 Sharing of radio frequency spectrum`

-- src:1313 | 14.—(1) Where a person (called the first person) is required under
-- src:1314 | this Act or any regulations made under this Act, to share with any
-- src:1315 | other person the radio frequency spectrum allocated to the first person
-- src:1316 | under a licence granted under section 5 or the grant of a spectrum
-- src:1317 | right under section 6, for a station or network —
-- src:1319 | (a) all persons operating on the shared radio frequency
-- src:1320 | spectrum must accept that interference may result from
-- src:1321 | the legitimate operation of the station or network specified
-- src:1322 | in the licence or the grant of a spectrum right; and
-- src:1324 | (b) the Authority is not responsible or liable for any
-- src:1325 | interference that may arise from the first person’s or
-- src:1326 | other person’s use of the shared radio frequency spectrum.
@ref s 14(1) (src:1313-1326)
GIVEN `the first person is required under this Act or regulations made under it to share the radio frequency spectrum allocated to it under a licence granted under section 5 or a spectrum right granted under section 6, for a station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1)(a): every person operating on the shared radio frequency spectrum must accept that interference may result from the legitimate operation of the station or network specified in the licence or grant` MEANS
    `the first person is required under this Act or regulations made under it to share the radio frequency spectrum allocated to it under a licence granted under section 5 or a spectrum right granted under section 6, for a station or network`

GIVEN `the first person is required under this Act or regulations made under it to share the radio frequency spectrum allocated to it under a licence granted under section 5 or a spectrum right granted under section 6, for a station or network` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(1)(b): the Authority is responsible or liable for interference arising from the first person's or another person's use of the shared spectrum` MEANS
    FALSE

-- src:1330 | (2) In subsection (1) —
-- src:1332 | “network” means 2 or more stations operated by a person and
-- src:1333 | used or intended to be used in communication with one
-- src:1334 | another;
-- src:1336 | “station” means —
-- src:1338 | (a) a transmitter;
-- src:1340 | (b) a receiver;
-- src:1342 | (c) a combination of transmitters and receivers; or
-- src:1344 | (d) an accessory to any thing specified in paragraphs (a),
-- src:1345 | (b) and (c).
@ref s 14(2) (src:1330-1345)
GIVEN `it is 2 or more stations operated by a person and used or intended to be used in communication with one another` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(2): this is a "network"` MEANS
    `it is 2 or more stations operated by a person and used or intended to be used in communication with one another`

GIVEN `it is a transmitter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a receiver` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a combination of transmitters and receivers` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an accessory to a transmitter, a receiver or a combination of them` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 14(2): this is a "station"` MEANS
    `it is a transmitter` OR `it is a receiver` OR `it is a combination of transmitters and receivers` OR `it is an accessory to a transmitter, a receiver or a combination of them`
